{"toolCallId":"call_5a45746e5b754caa928efe6ef9cc5f7b","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":"2:title: \"Implementation Plan: Add a quiet flag to recommend-level.sh\"\n3:description: \"Add a --quiet output mode to recommend-level.sh behind a shared level-line formatter, so the quiet line and the existing report line are the same bytes, and reject --quiet with --json.\"\n5:  - \"recommend level quiet flag plan\"\n10:# Implementation Plan: Add a quiet flag to recommend-level.sh\n30:`recommend-level.sh` gains a `--quiet` flag and one output function behind it. The level line moves into `format_level_line`, which the existing text report also calls, so the quiet line and the report line are the same bytes. A mode guard rejects `--quiet` with `--json`. Scoring, phase scoring and both existing output paths stay untouched.\n63:- **Argument parser (§5)**: owns flag parsing and usage errors. It gains one `--quiet` arm that sets `QUIET=true`.\n64:- **Mode guard**: one check after parsing that rejects `--quiet` with `--json` and exits 1.\n69:- **`output_quiet`**: prints `format_level_line` and nothing else.\n75:     → dispatch ─┬─ QUIET=true        → output_quiet\n81:The dispatch order matters: quiet is checked first, so the guard is the only thing standing between a caller and a mixed request. ADR-001 records why.\n95:| `recommend-level.sh` argument parser | Owns flag parsing and usage errors | update: add the `--quiet` arm and the mode guard | New test plus `--help` output |\n96:| `recommend-level.sh` header comment and `show_help` | Document the flags | update: add `--quiet` to both | `rg -n -- '--quiet' recommend-level.sh` |\n106:- Consumers of changed symbols: `rg -n 'recommend-level' .skilled/commands .skilled/hooks` returns two invocations (`speckit-plan.yaml:86`, `speckit-complete.yaml:147`), both `--json`, plus three prose notes. No consumer passes `--quiet` and none parses the text report.\n107:- Matrix axes: output mode (default, quiet, json, quiet plus json) x phase section (on, off) x input validity (valid, empty, non-numeric). The test covers the eight cells that differ; the rest are duplicates of an existing assertion.\n120:- **Phase 2 (Implementation)**: add the flag, the formatter, the quiet output path and the guard; update the help text; write the test and register it.\n131:| Unit | `format_level_line` and `output_quiet`, through a spawned script | `node:child_process` `execFileSync` in a smoke test |\n134:| Manual | `LEVEL=$(... --quiet)` in an interactive shell | bash |\n200:- [ ] No feature flag needed: `--quiet` is itself opt-in\n241:| `format_level_line` | Baseline | The one level-line renderer | `output_text` and `output_quiet` |\n242:| `--quiet` arm and guard | Parser globals | `QUIET` state and the mode error | `output_quiet` dispatch |\n243:| `output_quiet` | `format_level_line` | The single line | The quiet test |\n244:| New test | `output_quiet`, the guard | Pass or fail signal | Completion |\n253:2. **T006 formatter and quiet output path** - 30 minutes - CRITICAL\n272:| M2 | Flag and formatter in place | `--quiet` prints one line; default output still matches the baseline | End of Phase 2 |\n284:**Context**: The script has two output modes today, text and JSON. `--quiet` asks for one line of text. A caller can pass `--quiet` and `--json` in the same invocation, and the script has to do something: pick one mode, ignore one flag, or refuse.\n286:**Decision**: `--quiet` selects a third output mode that prints only `Recommended Level: <N> (<Name>)`. Combining it with `--json` exits 1 with `ERROR: --quiet cannot be combined with --json` on stderr. The quiet line is rendered by `format_level_line`, the same function the text report calls.\n290:- The quiet line cannot drift from the report line, because there is one renderer.\n295:- Silent precedence for `--quiet`: a caller that asked for JSON would receive text and a parser downstream would fail with a confusing message.\n296:- `--quiet` ignored in JSON mode: the flag becomes a silent no-op, the worst of the three options.\n"}}],"_meta":{"cognition.ai/cwd":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w4fbf614733/tree","terminal_exit":{"terminal_id":"a20f6f","exit_code":0,"signal":null},"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"exec"}}
{"toolCallId":"call_6a7dcd50776240e9b5777f1a5ac3fdcb","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":"16:// Dry by default; --apply writes. Everything --apply will write is named by the\n86:// graph-metadata.json itself. The others describe description.json contents and\n118:const USAGE = 'Usage: repair-derived.cjs [--folder <packet>]... [--roots <dir>] [--apply]';\n241:const REWRITE_TARGETS = ['description.json', 'graph-metadata.json', ...DOCS];\n259:  'description.json',\n326:    fs.writeFileSync(descriptor, text, 'utf8');\n347:  const file = path.join(folder, 'description.json');\n376:    what: `description level ${verb} -> ${level}`,\n411:  const description = path.join(folder, 'description.json');\n412:  const descriptionText = readIfPresent(description);\n413:  if (descriptionText !== null) {\n416:      data = JSON.parse(descriptionText);\n423:        file: description,\n424:        what: `description specFolder -> ${pointer}`,\n426:          const current = JSON.parse(readForWrite(description));\n428:          writeAtomic(description, `${JSON.stringify(current, null, 2)}\\n`);\n608:    if (token === '--apply') {\n620:      // turn a dropped flag name — `repair-derived.cjs specs/one --apply` —\n707:        // leave an --apply run without the account of what it already wrote.\n770:    process.stdout.write(`\\nTo apply these repairs:\\n  node ${path.relative(REPO, __filename)} ${scope} --apply\\n`);\n"}}],"_meta":{"cognition.ai/cwd":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w4fbf614733/tree","terminal_exit":{"terminal_id":"738eeb","exit_code":0,"signal":null},"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"exec"}}
{"toolCallId":"call_6f1bb0e4604b4c598eade7e28506e1d0","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":"---\n  \"confidence\": ${CONFIDENCE},\n  \"inputs\": {\n    \"loc\": ${LOC},\n    \"files\": ${FILES},\n    \"auth\": ${HAS_AUTH},\n    \"api\": ${HAS_API},\n    \"db\": ${HAS_DB},\n    \"architectural\": ${HAS_ARCHITECTURAL}\n  },\n  \"breakdown\": {\n    \"loc_score\": ${SCORE_LOC},\n    \"files_score\": ${SCORE_FILES},\n    \"risk_score\": ${SCORE_RISK},\n    \"complexity_score\": ${SCORE_COMPLEXITY},\n    \"details\": {\n      \"auth_points\": ${auth_points},\n      \"api_points\": ${api_points},\n      \"db_points\": ${db_points},\n      \"architectural_points\": ${arch_points}\n    }\n  },\n  \"thresholds\": {\n    \"level_0_max\": ${LEVEL_0_MAX},\n    \"level_1_max\": ${LEVEL_1_MAX},\n    \"level_2_max\": ${LEVEL_2_MAX}\n  }\n}\nEOF\n  fi\n}\n\n# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# 5. MAIN SCRIPT\n# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n# Parse command-line arguments\nwhile [[ $# -gt 0 ]]; do\n  case \"$1\" in\n    --loc)\n      if [[ -z \"${2:-}\" ]] || [[ \"$2\" =~ ^-- ]]; then\n        echo \"ERROR: --loc requires a numeric value\" >&2\n        exit 1\n      fi\n      LOC=\"$2\"\n      shift 2\n      ;;\n    --files)\n      if [[ -z \"${2:-}\" ]] || [[ \"$2\" =~ ^-- ]]; then\n        echo \"ERROR: --files requires a numeric value\" >&2\n        exit 1\n      fi\n      FILES=\"$2\"\n      shift 2\n      ;;\n    --auth)\n      HAS_AUTH=true\n      shift\n      ;;\n    --api)\n      HAS_API=true\n      shift\n      ;;\n    --db)\n      HAS_DB=true\n      shift\n      ;;\n    --architectural)\n      HAS_ARCHITECTURAL=true\n      shift\n      ;;\n    --recommend-phases)\n      RECOMMEND_PHASES=true\n      shift\n      ;;\n    --no-recommend-phases)\n      RECOMMEND_PHASES=false\n      shift\n      ;;\n    --phase-threshold)\n      if [[ -z \"${2:-}\" ]] || [[ \"$2\" =~ ^-- ]]; then\n        echo \"ERROR: --phase-threshold requires a numeric value\" >&2\n        exit 1\n      fi\n      PHASE_THRESHOLD=\"$2\"\n      shift 2\n      ;;\n    --json|-j)\n      JSON_OUTPUT=true\n      shift\n      ;;\n    --help|-h)\n      show_help\n      ;;\n    *)\n      echo \"ERROR: Unknown option: $1\" >&2\n      echo \"Use --help for usage information\" >&2\n      exit 1\n      ;;\n  esac\ndone\n\n# Validate numeric inputs first (before numeric comparison)\nif ! [[ \"$LOC\" =~ ^[0-9]+$ ]]; then\n  echo \"ERROR: --loc must be a positive integer\" >&2\n  exit 1\nfi\n\nif ! [[ \"$FILES\" =~ ^[0-9]+$ ]]; then\n  echo \"ERROR: --files must be a positive integer\" >&2\n  exit 1\nfi\n\nif ! [[ \"$PHASE_THRESHOLD\" =~ ^[0-9]+$ ]]; then\n  echo \"ERROR: --phase-threshold must be a positive integer\" >&2\n  exit 1\nfi\n\n# Validate required inputs\nif [[ \"$LOC\" -eq 0 ]] && [[ \"$FILES\" -eq 0 ]]; then\n  echo \"ERROR: At least --loc or --files must be provided\" >&2\n  echo \"Use --help for usage information\" >&2\n  exit 1\nfi\n\n# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# 6. CALCULATE SCORES\n# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\nSCORE_LOC=$(calculate_loc_score \"$LOC\")\nSCORE_FILES=$(calculate_files_score \"$FILES\")\nSCORE_RISK=$(calculate_risk_score)\nSCORE_COMPLEXITY=$(calculate_complexity_score)\n\nTOTAL_SCORE=$((SCORE_LOC + SCORE_FILES + SCORE_RISK + SCORE_COMPLEXITY))\n\n# Determine recommended level\ndetermine_level \"$TOTAL_SCORE\"\n\n# Calculate confidence\ncalculate_confidence\n\n"}}],"_meta":{"cognition.ai/cwd":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w4fbf614733/tree","terminal_exit":{"terminal_id":"4ce20d","exit_code":0,"signal":null},"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"exec"}}
