{"toolCallId":"call_e750ed9708184a9492ff9354d2cb8456","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":"9:// and the enforced run. It pairs with source_doc_hashes, a cheap freshness key so a strict run\n29:/** Validation rule id reported for the generated-metadata drift gate. */\n33:// derives from; the rest round out an honest freshness key so any source edit moves a hash.\n34:// Conservative by design: a hash change that is not a synopsis change only triggers a re-derive,\n64:  driftedFields: DriftedSynopsisField[];\n65:  /** Whether the persisted source_doc_hashes differ from the current source docs. */\n66:  hashDrift: boolean;\n67:  /** True when the folder predates the hash key, so it is reported as ungraded not in-sync. */\n72:/** A drift report resolved to a validator-consumable pass/error/info status and message. */\n87: * A doc edit changes its hash, giving the drift gate a cheap freshness key it can compare\n88: * before paying for a re-derive. Only present docs are hashed, so an absent doc carries no key\n89: * rather than a hash of empty content.\n96:  const hashes: Record<string, string> = {};\n101:      // A linked parent can expose another packet's source, so hash only local targets.\n107:    hashes[relativePath.replace(/\\\\/g, '/')] = crypto.createHash('sha256').update(content).digest('hex');\n109:  return hashes;\n162:  const value = (derived as Record<string, unknown>).source_doc_hashes;\n169:function hashMapsEqual(a: Record<string, string>, b: Record<string, string>): boolean {\n183: * Re-derive a spec folder and report whether its stored synopsis fields drifted from the docs.\n186: * the stored description and causal_summary. When the persisted source_doc_hashes match the\n187: * current docs the re-derive is skipped and no drift is reported, the cheap freshness key. A\n189: * drift, and an unreadable doc is reported as a read error rather than treated as in-sync. The\n193: * @returns The drift report with any drifted fields and the hash-freshness verdict\n204:    driftedFields: [],\n205:    hashDrift: false,\n215:  // Nothing stored to compare against: an authored-only folder is not scored as drift.\n236:      // No source doc to derive from: report an empty derivation, not drift.\n249:  const hashDrift = storedHashes !== null && !hashMapsEqual(storedHashes, currentHashes);\n251:  // Cheap freshness key: when the persisted hashes match the current docs nothing changed,\n252:  // so the re-derive is skipped and no field drift is possible.\n253:  if (storedHashes !== null && !hashDrift) {\n257:      driftedFields: [],\n258:      hashDrift: false,\n264:  const driftedFields: DriftedSynopsisField[] = [];\n272:      driftedFields.push({ field: 'description', stored: storedDescription, fresh });\n280:      driftedFields.push({ field: 'causal_summary', stored: storedCausalSummary, fresh });\n287:    driftedFields,\n288:    hashDrift,\n295: * Resolve a drift report into a single validation status given the rollout mode.\n297: * Under grandfather report mode any drift resolves to a non-blocking `info`, so a legacy folder\n301: * @param report - The drift report to resolve\n318:  const hasFindings = report.driftedFields.length > 0 || report.readErrors.length > 0;\n320:    const note = report.ungraded ? ' (ungraded, no source_doc_hashes yet)' : '';\n330:    ...report.driftedFields.map(\n331:      (drift) => `${drift.field}: stored '${drift.stored}' drifted from fresh '${drift.fresh}'`,\n339:    message: `Generated metadata drift found ${report.driftedFields.length} drifted field(s) (${mode})`,\n"}}],"_meta":{"cognition.ai/cwd":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w4fbf614733/tree","terminal_exit":{"terminal_id":"986e14","exit_code":0,"signal":null},"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"exec"}}
{"toolCallId":"call_ec37a3f921d44356b32c369a0645a988","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/lib/validation/README.md:17:`lib/validation/` decides every spec-folder rule verdict. It detects a folder's documentation level, runs the named spec-doc structure rules, checks the two generated JSON files (`description.json` and `graph-metadata.json`) against their schemas and invariants, and folds the results into the `ValidationReport` that `validate.sh` prints.\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/lib/validation/README.md:23:- `generated-metadata-integrity.ts` validates `description.json` and `graph-metadata.json` against the shared Zod schemas plus the canonical path-prefix and status-enum invariants. Severity resolution is left to the caller, so the same check backs both the grandfather report-mode rollout and the enforced run.\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/lib/validation/README.md:48:| `generated-metadata-integrity.ts` | Schema, path-prefix, and status-enum validation for `description.json` and `graph-metadata.json`. |\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/lib/validation/generated-metadata-integrity.ts:5:// description.json and graph-metadata.json. It runs the shared Zod schemas plus the\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/lib/validation/generated-metadata-integrity.ts:37:export type GeneratedMetadataFile = 'graph-metadata.json' | 'description.json';\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/lib/validation/generated-metadata-integrity.ts:303:      file: 'description.json',\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/lib/validation/generated-metadata-integrity.ts:305:      message: `description.json could not be ${read.reason === 'unreadable' ? 'read' : 'parsed as JSON'}`,\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/lib/validation/generated-metadata-integrity.ts:315:      violations.push({ file: 'description.json', code: 'SCHEMA_INVALID', message: `${location}: ${issue.message}` });\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/lib/validation/generated-metadata-integrity.ts:322:      file: 'description.json',\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/lib/validation/generated-metadata-integrity.ts:347:  const descriptionPath = path.join(folder, 'description.json');\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/lib/validation/generated-metadata-integrity.ts:363:      message: 'graph-metadata.json is missing while description.json is present',\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/lib/validation/generated-metadata-integrity.ts:371:      file: 'description.json',\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/lib/validation/generated-metadata-integrity.ts:373:      message: 'description.json is missing while graph-metadata.json is present',\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/lib/validation/orchestrator.ts:652:    for (const required of ['description.json', 'graph-metadata.json']) {\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/lib/utils/index-scope.ts:192:// Authoritative z_future exclusion for generated metadata (description.json and\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/lib/resume/resume-ladder.ts:271:    && (fs.existsSync(path.join(childPath, 'spec.md')) || fs.existsSync(path.join(childPath, 'description.json')));\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/lib/spec/is-phase-parent.ts:7://   2. ≥1 such child has spec.md OR description.json\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/lib/spec/is-phase-parent.ts:25:  /** Whether the child carries spec.md or description.json (the phase-parent qualifier). */\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/lib/spec/is-phase-parent.ts:34: * the ones carrying spec.md or description.json. `isPhaseParent` reads `qualifies` while the\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/lib/spec/is-phase-parent.ts:54:        || fs.existsSync(path.join(childPath, 'description.json'));\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/lib/spec/is-phase-parent.ts:81:/** Whether a folder qualifies as a phase parent: at least one phase-child directory carries spec.md or description.json. */\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/lib/spec/is-phase-parent.ts:111:      fs.existsSync(path.join(childPath, 'description.json'))\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/lib/spec/is-phase-parent.ts:121:// has spec.md/description.json. Counting all NNN-named direct children\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/lib/spec/README.md:16:`lib/spec/` owns the single detection rule for phase-parent folders, so no caller re-implements the traversal. A folder is a phase parent when it has at least one direct child matching `^[0-9]{3}-[a-z0-9][a-z0-9-]*$` and at least one such child carries `spec.md` or `description.json`.\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/lib/config/spec-doc-paths.ts:28:  'description.json',\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/lib/config/spec-doc-paths.ts:64:// deliberately creates description.json/graph-metadata.json inside\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/lib/config/spec-doc-paths.ts:187:  // The research-metadata backfill places description.json inside\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/lib/config/spec-doc-paths.ts:189:  if (normalizedBasename === 'description.json' && parent === 'iterations') {\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/lib/config/spec-doc-paths.ts:324: * One source of identity for both the description.json and graph-metadata.json\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/lib/README.md:71:| Generated metadata | `graph/`, `description/`, `search/` | Derive, merge, write and gate `graph-metadata.json` and `description.json`. |\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/lib/README.md:86:├── description/     # description.json schema, merge, synopsis and repair\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/lib/README.md:117:| `spec/is-phase-parent.ts` | Single-source-of-truth phase-parent detection: a numbered child that carries `spec.md` or `description.json`. |\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/lib/config/capability-flags.ts:77: * restamped the legacy description.json and graph-metadata.json files, so the\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/lib/MODULE-MAP.md:64:- Purpose: Owns `description.json`: its schema, the merge rule that preserves authored keys, and the shared synopsis extractor.\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/lib/MODULE-MAP.md:135:  - `is-phase-parent.ts` — a folder is a phase parent when it has at least one `^[0-9]{3}-[a-z0-9][a-z0-9-]*$` child and at least one such child carries `spec.md` or `description.json`.\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/lib/MODULE-MAP.md:275:- Rule: both generated summary fields — `description` in `description.json` and `causal_summary` in `graph-metadata.json` — derive from this one extractor with a per-field length limit, so they move together against the same source document.\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/lib/search/README.md:22:- It owns both sides of `description.json`: generation and save, load with a typed result, staleness detection, and merge-preserving repair.\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/lib/search/README.md:41:│ graph/       │ ───▶ │ description.json │      │ parsing/        │\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/lib/search/README.md:103:| Schema ownership | The `description.json` schema and merge rule belong to `lib/description/`. This folder calls them; it does not restate them. |\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/lib/search/README.md:126:│ merge over any authored description.json  │\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/lib/search/README.md:143:| `savePerFolderDescription()` | Function | Writes `description.json` for a folder. |\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/lib/search/README.md:149:| `getRepairMergeSafe()` | Function | Whether description.json repairs preserve unrecognized authored keys (`SPECKIT_DESCRIPTION_REPAIR_MERGE_SAFE`). |\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/lib/search/folder-discovery.ts:54: * Per-folder description stored as `description.json` inside each spec folder.\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/lib/search/folder-discovery.ts:70:/** Outcome of loading a packet's description.json: the parsed record, or why it could not be loaded. */\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/lib/search/folder-discovery.ts:293:    console.warn(`Warning: description.json parse error, writing minimal replacement${detail}`);\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/lib/search/folder-discovery.ts:299:/** Whether saving `desc` for `folderPath` would actually change the on-disk description.json. */\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/lib/search/folder-discovery.ts:304:  const descPath = path.join(folderPath, 'description.json');\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/lib/search/folder-discovery.ts:314:/** Whether description.json repairs preserve unrecognized authored keys instead of overwriting them. */\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/lib/search/folder-discovery.ts:413: * Read and parse a per-folder description.json into a raw record for comparison.\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/lib/search/folder-discovery.ts:572:        // Also check description.json mtime so aggregate cache staleness\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/lib/search/folder-discovery.ts:575:          const descPath = path.join(discoveredFolder.folderPath, 'description.json');\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/lib/search/folder-discovery.ts:888:      const descPath = path.join(discoveredFolder.folderPath, 'description.json');\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/lib/search/folder-discovery.ts:890:      // Prefer per-folder description.json if fresh and non-empty. Blank-description edge\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/lib/search/folder-discovery.ts:956: * Batch repair stale description.json files.\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/lib/search/folder-discovery.ts:1072: * Preserves memorySequence and memoryNameHistory from existing description.json.\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/lib/search/folder-discovery.ts:1111:  // Preserve existing tracking data if description.json already exists\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/lib/search/folder-discovery.ts:1132: * Load a PerFolderDescription from `description.json` in the given folder.\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/lib/search/folder-discovery.ts:1135: * merges what it reads into the packet's own description.json.\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/lib/search/folder-discovery.ts:1141:  const descPath = path.join(folderPath, 'description.json');\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/lib/search/folder-discovery.ts:1176:/** Load a folder's description.json, returning null when absent or invalid. */\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/lib/search/folder-discovery.ts:1183: * Save a PerFolderDescription to `description.json` using atomic write.\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/lib/search/folder-discovery.ts:1207:  const descPath = path.join(folderPath, 'description.json');\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/lib/search/folder-discovery.ts:1244: * Check whether a per-folder description.json is stale.\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/lib/search/folder-discovery.ts:1245: * Compares description.json mtime vs spec.md mtime.\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/lib/search/folder-discovery.ts:1246: * Missing description.json = stale.\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/lib/search/folder-discovery.ts:1249: * @returns true if description.json is missing or older than spec.md.\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/lib/search/folder-discovery.ts:1252:  const descPath = path.join(folderPath, 'description.json');\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/lib/description/packet-synopsis.ts:5:// folder: the description in description.json and the causal_summary in graph-metadata.json.\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/lib/description/description-schema.ts:115:/** Whether a description.json key is one of the schema's reserved (derived, authored, or tracking) keys. */\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/lib/description/description-schema.ts:120:/** Extract only the canonical derived and authored fields from a raw description.json object. */\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/lib/graph/generated-metadata-drift.ts:5:// derivation, so a description.json or graph-metadata.json that fell out of sync with the docs\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/lib/graph/generated-metadata-drift.ts:199:  const descriptionPath = path.join(folder, 'description.json');\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/lib/graph/generated-metadata-drift.ts:225:    readErrors.push(`description.json could not be ${descriptionRead.reason === 'unreadable' ? 'read' : 'parsed as JSON'}`);\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/lib/description/README.md:6:  - \"description.json repair\"\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/lib/description/README.md:19:- Defines the accepted `description.json` shape with `zod` schemas.\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/lib/description/README.md:22:- The schema-error repair path (a `description.json` that fails schema validation) calls `mergeDescription` directly from `lib/search/folder-discovery.ts`; the folder previously also carried a `repair.ts` wrapper over the same call, but nothing but its own tests ever used it, so it was removed rather than kept as an unused second path to the same merge.\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/lib/description/description-merge.ts:12:/** Outcome of merging a description.json payload: the merged object plus which keys came from where. */\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/lib/description/description-merge.ts:49: * Merge an existing description.json with freshly derived canonical fields and\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/lib/description/description-merge.ts:52: * @param existing - The description.json currently on disk, or null when absent\n"}}],"_meta":{"cognition.ai/cwd":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-